---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Docs"
  description="Installation, LinkedIn app setup, authentication, and every postiee command with its flags."
>
  <p class="eyebrow">Documentation</p>
  <h1>Docs</h1>

  <p class="lead">
    Install it, create a LinkedIn app, log in, post. About ten minutes the first
    time, seconds after that.
  </p>

  <h2>Install</h2>

  <p><strong>macOS and Linux</strong></p>
  <pre><code>curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aswathas/postiee/main/install.sh | sh</code></pre>

  <p><strong>Windows (PowerShell)</strong></p>
  <pre><code>irm https://raw.githubusercontent.com/aswathas/postiee/main/install.ps1 | iex</code></pre>

  <p><strong>From source</strong> — needs Go 1.26.9 or newer:</p>
  <pre><code>git clone https://github.com/aswathas/postiee.git
cd postiee
go build -o postiee ./cmd/postiee
sudo mv postiee /usr/local/bin/</code></pre>

  <p>
    The installers detect your OS and CPU, prefer a per-user location so no
    admin rights are needed, and warn if the install directory is not on
    <code>PATH</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Create a LinkedIn app</h2>

  <ol>
    <li>
      Go to <a href="https://www.linkedin.com/developers/apps">linkedin.com/developers/apps</a>
      and click <strong>Create app</strong>.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Products</strong> tab → add <strong>Share on LinkedIn</strong>.
      This grants <code>w_member_social</code>. Self-serve, no review.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Products</strong> tab → add <strong>Sign In with LinkedIn</strong>.
      This grants <code>openid</code> and <code>profile</code>. You need it to
      resolve your own member ID.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Auth</strong> tab → add this exact redirect URL:
      <pre><code>http://localhost:8085/callback</code></pre>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <p class="note warn">
    LinkedIn matches redirect URLs as <strong>exact strings</strong>. If you
    registered <code>localhost</code> and the CLI sends <code>127.0.0.1</code>,
    login fails with <em>"redirect_uri does not match the registered value"</em>.
    Set <code>POSTIEE_REDIRECT_URI</code> to match whatever you registered.
  </p>

  <h2>Add your credentials</h2>

  <p>
    Write them to a file rather than passing them as flags — a flag value lands
    in your shell history and in process listings.
  </p>

  <pre><code>mkdir -p ~/.config/postiee
chmod 700 ~/.config/postiee

cat > ~/.config/postiee/credentials.toml &lt;&lt;EOF
client_id = "your_client_id"
client_secret = "your_client_secret"
EOF

chmod 600 ~/.config/postiee/credentials.toml</code></pre>

  <p>
    On Windows the same file lives at
    <code>%USERPROFILE%\.config\postiee\credentials.toml</code>.
  </p>

  <h2>Log in</h2>

  <pre><code>postiee auth login --port 8085</code></pre>

  <p>
    Your browser opens, you approve, and the token is stored. It lasts 60 days.
    Programmatic refresh is reserved for LinkedIn partners, so after expiry you
    re-run <code>auth login</code>; the consent screen is skipped if you are
    still signed in.
  </p>

  <h2>Commands</h2>

  <h3>post</h3>
  <pre><code>postiee post "some text"
postiee post --file post.md
postiee post "with a picture" --image chart.png --alt "a line chart"
postiee post "connections only" -v CONNECTIONS</code></pre>
  <p>
    Visibility is <code>PUBLIC</code>, <code>CONNECTIONS</code>, or
    <code>LOGGED_IN</code>. Prefer <code>--file</code> for long posts — it
    avoids shell quoting entirely.
  </p>

  <h3>history</h3>
  <pre><code>postiee history
postiee history --limit 200</code></pre>
  <p>Every post recorded locally, newest first.</p>

  <h3>search</h3>
  <pre><code>postiee search harness
postiee search "harness agent" --json</code></pre>
  <p>
    Terms are ANDed. Porter stemming is on, so <code>authentic</code> finds
    <code>authentication</code>.
  </p>
  <p class="note warn">
    <strong>Partial-word prefixes do not work.</strong> SQLite FTS5 indexes
    whole tokens, so <code>search harn</code> will not find
    <code>harness</code>. Use the full word.
  </p>

  <h3>forget</h3>
  <pre><code>postiee forget urn:li:ugcPost:12345</code></pre>
  <p>Removes a post from your local history. Does not delete it on LinkedIn.</p>

  <h3>auth and doctor</h3>
  <pre><code>postiee auth status
postiee auth logout
postiee doctor</code></pre>
  <p>
    <code>doctor</code> checks config, credentials, and that
    <code>api.linkedin.com</code> is reachable.
  </p>

  <h2>Agent mode</h2>
  <pre><code>postiee --agent search harness</code></pre>
  <p>
    Sets <code>--json --compact --no-input --no-color</code> together. Use it
    whenever you are parsing output.
  </p>

  <h2>Environment variables</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Variable</th>
        <th scope="col">Effect</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>POSTIEE_SCOPES</code></td>
        <td>
          Override the requested OAuth scopes. Use during setup when your app
          only has <code>w_member_social</code> and you have not added Sign In
          yet.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>POSTIEE_REDIRECT_URI</code></td>
        <td>
          Override the redirect host spelling. Must match your app's
          registration exactly.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>POSTIEE_TOKEN</code></td>
        <td>Use a specific access token instead of the stored one.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>POSTIEE_HISTORY_DB</code></td>
        <td>Point the history database somewhere else.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Troubleshooting</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">Error</th>
        <th scope="col">Fix</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>unauthorized_scope_error</code></td>
        <td>
          A requested scope is not granted to your app. Add the product, or
          narrow the request with <code>POSTIEE_SCOPES</code>.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>redirect_uri does not match</code></td>
        <td>
          Set <code>POSTIEE_REDIRECT_URI</code> to exactly what is registered in
          your Auth tab.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>403 … userinfo</code></td>
        <td>
          <code>openid</code> is not yet active. Add Sign In with LinkedIn, wait
          about an hour for propagation, then <code>auth logout</code> and log in
          again.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>422 … /author</code></td>
        <td>
          Your app lacks <code>openid</code>, so the member URN cannot be
          resolved.
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Nothing found by <code>search</code></td>
        <td>
          You searched a partial word. FTS5 matches whole tokens only — try
          <code>harness</code> rather than <code>harn</code>.
        </td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Rate limit</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>150 requests per day per member.</strong> One post is one request.
    A script that loops will hit this, and the symptom looks like an unrelated
    error rather than a limit.
  </p>

  <h2>Where files live</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th scope="col">What</th>
        <th scope="col">macOS / Linux</th>
        <th scope="col">Windows</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Credentials</td>
        <td><code>~/.config/postiee/</code></td>
        <td><code>%USERPROFILE%\.config\postiee\</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Token</td>
        <td><code>~/.local/share/postiee/</code></td>
        <td><code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\postiee\</code></td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>History</td>
        <td><code>~/.config/postiee/history.db</code></td>
        <td><code>%USERPROFILE%\.config\postiee\history.db</code></td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</Base>